  "findings": [],
  "assessment": [
    "Every spawned serving task is synchronously stored in the coordinator JoinSet; enclosing ConnectionPeer Drop requests coordinator abort, and JoinSet Drop requests descendant abort.",
    "Both accept and actual pending observe are selected against stop while cancel-safe join_next retains completed sibling results. Worker select polls actual serve first; only successful private stop is intentional success. All unexpected JoinError cancellation/panic and receiver-disconnection errors are retained.",
    "The shared five-second drain keeps accumulated outcomes outside the timed future. Earlier failures survive Elapsed; remaining tasks receive Drop abort without a beyond-budget join claim.",
    "finish_after captures the actual operation result. finish_result skips count waits on operation failure, stops QUIC and TCP, observes both results, combines both cleanup causes and preserves exact client primary. Clients remain alive across explicit cleanup.",
    "Seven ordinary request sequences reconstruct after only preparation placement and result capture; assertions, wire/profile/route operations, response bodies and SETTLE remain exact. Existing protocol helper bodies and all five child blobs remain exact."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Source-only; no Cargo, compiler, lint, format, test, import, socket or process execution by reviewer.",
    "Results accumulate in completion-observation order, not connection order; handshake metadata remains in acceptance order.",
    "External cancellation before a completed cause is observed can abort outstanding work; Drop does not synchronously join or guarantee returned typed outcomes.",
    "TCP broad TLS/head/write/shutdown/accept classifications remain unchanged and outside this QUIC slice.",
    "Unchanged eight controls require root native verification; no final A180/A181, production leak, browser, full architecture, integration-gate or merge approval."
  ],
  "required_root_verification": "Run unchanged eight QUIC controls, seven ordinary methods, count/deadline/TCP regressions on both hosts; targeted cargo fmt, strict Clippy and Rust 1.88 checks, then applicable full integration gates. No vendor source changed."
}
